========================================================================
================== CFD toy solver using ISFFT ==========================
========================================================================
# nx_global, ny_global, nz_global, Dimension, Boundary (Periodic: 0, Dirichlet: 1, Neumann: 2)
    128         128        128         3         0  0  0
#  npx0, npy0, npz0, LAP
    2     2     1     0
#  SLx,    SLy,    SLz
   4.0     4.0     4.0
#  Repeat_count (number of Poisson solver calls)
           1
#  Decomposition (Block:0, Slab:1, Pencil:2)
           1
#  Scheme_type (0 Spectral, 1 E2, 2 E4, 3 C4, 4 E6, 5 C6, 6 Spectral-like)
           0
========================================================================
# Each active Boundary combination defines one analytical test.
# P: cos(2*pi*x/L), D: sin(pi*x/L), N: cos(pi*x/L); phi is their product.
# Inactive directions require grid size and process count equal to 1.
